From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 22:11:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] null renderer: RGBA8 writes and bilinear filtering in arrays,
 sRGB in the fast path, fragment shaders' own depth

A block's pixels in a block-linear RGBA8 render target are two runs of 32 bytes (4 columns
by 2 rows, as a GOB keeps them; blocks now start on 4 columns): their colours are
converted, blended by source alpha and stored in loops the compiler vectorizes, where each
pixel was addressed, converted and blended on its own. Bilinear filtering does two channels
in each 32-bit multiply, and sRGB textures, which went one lane at a time, are decoded
through their table and filtered in floats in the fast path.

A fragment shader that writes its own depth gets the depth test after it, with that depth;
the interpolated depth was used.
